WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.770
- I'm going to take a quiz and find out

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.210
how Irish I am, or I'm going to make my

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.448
Irish ancestors roll in their graves.

00:00:07.448 --> 00:00:10.180
(jaunty Irish music)

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.660
- My mom did a DNA test
about two years ago and

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.520
found out that she is literally
50% English and 50% Irish.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.940
- I'm descended from the
Duke of Abbot who was

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.250
an heir to the throne
back in 14th century.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.030
- My great-grandmother, Frances,

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.490
came over on a boat from Ireland.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.380
- I am not very culturally Irish.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.780
- I have green hair.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.340
- I do drink a lot of beer though.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.290
- The answer's no, not
culturally Irish at all.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.540
What is the significance
of St. Patrick's Day?

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.140
- Oh God, what did Saint Patrick do?

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.270
- Ooh, okay.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.830
- He's like Santa's brother
or something, Saint Nick.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.280
- The Catholics versus the Protestants.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.300
- There were snakes.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.830
- The snakes are
Protestants; it's a metaphor.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.660
- Saint Patrick drove all of
the snakes out of Ireland.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.010
- St. Patrick's Day is March 17th.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.510
- It's March 17th, I know that.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.580
- I believe it is the
second Sunday in March.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.223
- Which of the following
is not a place in Ireland?

00:01:01.223 --> 00:01:02.480
- Doodys Bottoms

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.313
- Slutsend

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.560
- Muff (laughs)

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.393
- Clitheroe

00:01:05.393 --> 00:01:06.230
- Or, Cum?

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.910
- Wow! Don't show my mom
this, this is so dirty.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:13.253
Okay, this is the city I
don't think exists in Ireland.

00:01:14.165 --> 00:01:16.590
- Clitheroe is in
England, that makes sense.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.100
Pronounce the following names (sighs)

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.440
This is where it all falls apart.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.360
- Shi-vawn

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.193
- Show-bin

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:23.026
- [Interviewer] Shi-vawn.

00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:24.070
- Shi-vawn?

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.060
- Shi-bawn I know, that one I have.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.770
- That's how you guys spell Siobhan?

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.630
- Nam?

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:29.463
- Ny-me

00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:30.296
- Nee-um?

00:01:30.296 --> 00:01:31.129
- [Interviewer] Neev.

00:01:31.129 --> 00:01:31.962
- Neev?

00:01:31.962 --> 00:01:33.180
- Oh of course, yeah.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.570
- Cay-ohm, no.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.002
- Cave?

00:01:36.002 --> 00:01:37.229
- Cay-o-heem?

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.287
- Ky-eev? (laughs)

00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:39.232
- [Interviewer] Nailing it.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.306
- Celeste? (laughs)

00:01:40.306 --> 00:01:41.139
- [Interviewer] Quee-va.

00:01:41.139 --> 00:01:41.972
- Quee-va?

00:01:41.972 --> 00:01:43.040
- (laughs) Of course it is.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.750
- Spell the following names.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.680
- This is going to be bad;
I can't spell anything.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.695
- [Interviewer] The first name is Aoife.

00:01:49.695 --> 00:01:50.610
- Ee-fa.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.410
- I've never felt so defeated in my life,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.950
and I've taken three Bar Exams.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.410
- Now if I know anything
about Gaelic, it's that

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.823
the letters do not
correspond to the sounds.

00:02:02.104 --> 00:02:03.520
- Sive.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.483
- S-I-E

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.283
- Sive.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:13.700
Hold on, say it again, who's right?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.490
- Name three Irish celebrities.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.420
- Saoirse Ronan.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.760
- Is Liam Neeson Irish?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.593
- Liam Neeson.

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:19.426
- Bono.

00:02:19.426 --> 00:02:20.259
- Oh, Bono!

00:02:20.259 --> 00:02:21.180
- Someone from Game of Thrones.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.013
- Saoirse Ronan.

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:23.350
- Is Colin Farrell Irish?

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.230
- Colin Farrell?

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.210
- Do I get half a point for just knowing

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.820
that the guy who was in In Bruges

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.583
who is not Colin Farrell is, wait,

00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:33.480
oh is Colin Farrell, is he Irish? Yes!

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.620
- Read these lyrics in an Irish accent.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.360
I knew I was going to have
to do an Irish accent.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.810
- There is not enough alcohol in the world

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.100
to get me to do this, I am sorry.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.240
- [Interviewer] Try,
just commit. Two lines.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.070
- I mean, I could sing this song.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.323
Let's do it in the style of

00:02:44.323 --> 00:02:46.264
Littlefinger from Game of Thrones.

00:02:46.264 --> 00:02:49.434
♪Oh, Danny boy, the pipes,
the pipes are calling ♪

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:52.506
♪From glen to glen, and
down the mountain side ♪

00:02:52.506 --> 00:02:55.863
♪The summer's gone,
all the roses falling ♪

00:02:55.863 --> 00:02:56.696
(record scratches)

00:02:56.696 --> 00:02:58.404
- I'm so so sorry.

00:02:58.404 --> 00:03:01.531
♪It'll be there in sunshine or shadow ♪

00:03:01.531 --> 00:03:05.220
♪Oh, Danny boy, oh Danny
boy, I love you so! ♪

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.320
- I did better than I thought.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.800
The song at the end really
kind of put me over the top.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.613
- Hey! Do they raise the roof in Ireland?

00:03:11.613 --> 00:03:15.250
- 33 ish percent or so, I'll take it.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.300
- Everyone who's watching from Ireland,

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.600
I just want to say that I'm sorry.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.433
- I'm sorry.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.186
- I'm so sorry, I really--

00:03:23.186 --> 00:03:25.720
- I do claim Irish heritage, but

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.550
apparently I have not earned it.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.120
- You're a beautiful country with

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.260
a lot of culture, and
you have given so much--

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.618
- Please don't hold this video against me.

00:03:34.618 --> 00:03:37.535
(slow Irish music)

